cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this data, cite the organizational author below and link to
  https://www.daily-life-hacks.com/methodology/ so readers can check the
  priced month and the row-level sources. The original Daily Life Hacks
  selection, arrangement, calculations, field descriptions, and explanatory
  material are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International.
  Upstream facts and third-party material keep their own status and terms.
  Full scope: https://www.daily-life-hacks.com/data-reuse/
title: Daily Life Hacks Food Value Data
type: dataset
version: "2026.3"
date-released: "2026-07-31"
abstract: >-
  US grocery prices paired with USDA nutrient values, covering fiber per
  dollar, protein per dollar, protein quality adjusted with DIAAS, daily menu
  costing, and category rankings. Nutrient values come from USDA FoodData
  Central where a row names an FDC id. Prices are US national figures: BLS
  Average Price data where the item is tracked, retailer listings otherwise.
  The priced month recorded across those price_basis fields is July 2026.
  Rankings are as-purchased, with USDA refuse removed where the row says so.
  The original Daily Life Hacks contribution is licensed under Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International. Source facts and third-party material
  are not relicensed.
license: CC-BY-4.0
